<article class="env-lemma" id="09VY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09VY">Lemma <span data-tag="09VY">25.6.5</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site with equalizers and fibre products. Let $K$ be a hypercovering. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian sheaf. There is a spectral sequence $(E_ r, d_ r)_{r \geq 0}$ with </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  E_2^{p, q} = \check{H}^ p(K, \underline{H}^ q(\mathcal{F}))  \]
</div>
  <p> converging to the global cohomology groups $H^{p + q}(\mathcal{F})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/09VX" data-tag="09VX">25.6.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>